+=head2 Hard-wrapped matches
+
+Matches spanning rows that were wrapped by the terminal itself are handled
+transparently. Programs that wrap output on their own (pagers, mail and
+feed readers, markdown renderers, full screen applications) emit separate
+rows instead, which splits a long URL into two or more matches.
+
+With the C<matcher.join-wrapped> resource enabled, a match that ends at the
+last non-blank column of a row that is as wide as the longest visible row is
+joined with the leading token of the following row, as long as the result
+still matches the pattern. The joined text is used for the launcher and
+the rendition, the rows are displayed unchanged. Leading whitespace on the
+continuation row is skipped, wrap markers (such as the C<+> of neomutt) are
+not and should be disabled in the application.
+
+    URxvt.matcher.join-wrapped: true
+
